title gravity (AutumnBench port)
author ported from AutumnBench gravity.sexp

(
  Port of AutumnBench gravity.sexp (GRID_SIZE=16).

  Autumn render_all keys: leftButton, rightButton, upButton, downButton, blobs.

  Mechanics:
  - 4 colored buttons at fixed edge positions change gravity direction.
  - Clicking empty space spawns a 2x2 blob: top-left at (cx,cy-1) where (cx,cy)=click.
  - All blobs move 1 cell per frame in current gravity direction.
  - Blobs fall off the grid (Autumn: no wall collision; PS: blocked at border).

  Blob types encode gravity direction:
    BlobDown  = falling down  (initial)
    BlobUp    = falling up
    BlobLeft  = falling left
    BlobRight = falling right

  Gravity direction stored as one of GravDown/GravLeft/GravRight/GravUp at (0,0).
  Spawn produces the matching blob type via global two-cell rules.
  Gravity button clicks:
    - Change GravX to new GravY (global two-cell rule)
    - Transform all existing BlobX cells to new BlobY type (global two-cell rules)

  Spawn sequence (fires AFTER gravity movement, per Autumn rule order):
    Anchor: [GravX] [action Player no BlobX no BlobSeedHere] -> place BlobX VM BlobSeedHere
    Up spread: place BlobX VM above BlobSeedHere
    Right spread: place BlobX VM BlobSeedR to right of BlobSeedHere
    Upper-right: place BlobX VM above BlobSeedR
    VM on spawn: prevents gravity from moving newly-spawned blobs same tick.

  PS cursor conventions: Player is invisible, moves with arrows, action = click.
  cursor_start=[0,0]. Buttons NOT blocked (different collision layer from Player).

  Deferred: off-grid motion (PS border blocks, Autumn allows off-grid).
)

realtime_interval 0.1

